And in `_onShellJobSettled` (waiting ext): `unawaited(_waiting.jobSettled(job))` → waiting-row leave; then `if (!job.notifyOnSettle) return;` → `io.writeln('[bash] <id> exited(0)…')` → `if (_exited || fence) return;`. So the `[bash] exited` line still prints (bookkeeping). Good.

